source: https://www.recipetineats.com/skirt-steak-with-chimichurri-sauce/
yield: makes 3/4 cup
ingredients:
  - item: parsley leaves
    qty: 1
    unit: cup
    note: tightly packed
  - item: oregano leaves
    qty: 1
    unit: tbsp
    optional: true
    note: tightly packed; still lovely without
  - item: garlic
    qty: 4
    unit: clove
    note: minced
  - item: red pepper flakes
    optional: true
    note: 0-2 tsp, adjust to taste
  - item: red wine vinegar
    qty: 0.25
    unit: cup
    note: 65 ml
  - item: salt
    qty: 0.5
    unit: tsp
  - black pepper
  - item: extra virgin olive oil
    qty: 0.5
    unit: cup
    note: 125 ml
steps:
  - place all ingredients except oil in a food processor
  - whizz until parsley is finely chopped, but not pureed (or chop parsley by hand)
  - transfer into a small bowl, add oil, gently stir
  - set aside for 1 hour before use, overnight is even better
notes: |
  Store in an airtight container in the fridge and use within 3 days. Freezes well.
  Red wine vinegar can be substituted with sherry vinegar or other mild vinegar —
  don't use balsamic or normal white vinegar, too harsh.
  From a skirt steak recipe: 700g flat iron/flank/skirt at room temp, salt and pepper,
  2 mins per side for medium-rare (2.5 for medium), rest 5-10 mins, slice against the grain.
